!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = actue myeloid luekemia
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: MOLM-13 cell
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: day 5 after sgNeg2 guideRNA infection
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = chip antibody: none
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Cells were lentivirally infected with sgRNA for knockout, or treated with DMSO or 100 nM HG-9-91-01 for 2 hrs
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Cells were cultured in RPMI with 10% FBS and penicillin/streptomycin.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Cell lysates were clarified from sonicated nuclei and histone-DNA complexes were isolated with antibody.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Libraries were prepared using Illumina TruSeq ChIP Sample Prep kit following manufacture's protocol. Briefly, ChIP DNA was end-repaired, 3’-adenylated, and then ligated with indexed adaptor. These DNA was size selected (200-400 bp) via agarose gel electrophoresis, and PCR amplified. Final products were purified using AMPure XP beads.
!Sample_data_processing = Sequencing reads were mapped into reference human genome hg19 using Bowtie2
!Sample_data_processing = Peakcalling was done using MACS2 FDR cut off 5% with broad peak and narrow peak option for H3K27ac and MEF2C, respectively
!Sample_data_processing = The H3K27ac peaks in knockout experiment or HG-9-91-01 treatment experiment were merged with corresponding control ChIP-seq using BEDtools
!Sample_data_processing = Normalized tag count was calculated using Bamliquidator package
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: hg19
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: bigwig
